# C3 substrate hardening fragment — bare-metal-uefi ONLY. Merged AFTER kernel-hardening.config by
# build-kernel.sh as the substrate fragment (KernelInputs.substrate_fragment for BareMetalUefi). The
# vps-kvm counterpart (kernel-hardening-vpskvm.config) DISABLES this stack instead.
#
# --- USB host/storage stack (bare-metal SB validation boots off USB media) ---
# The linux-virt base ships these as modules (USB=m, USB_STORAGE=m), which MODULES=n
# promotes to =y builtin; force =y anyway to PIN the requirement (a base drift to =n would otherwise
# silently drop the stack bare-metal boots off). Real bare-metal boots off a USB disk whose enumeration
# needs the xHCI/EHCI host controllers + the USB mass-storage driver; without them the boot disk is
# invisible in /sys/block and PARTUUID resolution fails. (The SCSI/sd + SATA stack USB-storage rides on is
# shared base config — now force-set + PINNED in kernel-hardening.config per audit L-1 — so it is not
# duplicated here.)
#
# FORWARD-DEBT (audit R2-Info, bare-metal production close-out): the PCI USB glue this stack rides on —
# USB_PCI (+ USB_XHCI_PCI) — is currently only `=y` via Kconfig `default y`, NOT explicitly
# pinned here (asymmetric with vps-kvm's explicit force-DISABLE + assert of USB_PCI). A base drift to
# `default n` would silently break USB boot on a PCI xHCI controller. Pin them explicitly when the
# bare-metal-uefi arm gets its first produced-bytes (UEFI) proof — don't pin an unproven arm blind here.
CONFIG_USB=y
CONFIG_USB_XHCI_HCD=y
CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
CONFIG_USB_STORAGE=y
